ables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-statuses-stat-stages-and-immunities.md","start":185,"end":185},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp40-commands-obedience-and-action-order.md","start":171,"end":171},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp42-growth-end-of-round-and-battle-outcomes.md","start":150,"end":150},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp43-types-accuracy-and-damage.md","start":130,"end":130}],"behavioral_fact":"Charge starts at 2. Normal round-tail processing can reduce it to 1. Reaching the end-of-action cleanup clears exactly count 1 before later Instruct/Dancer processing; count 2 is not cleared by that action cleanup. The clear is not conditional on having used an Electric move or on successfully dealing damage.","prerequisites":["Default Charge was successfully used; no special ability/item/state callbacks alter the counter.","Both sides remain able to battle; a later ordinary move attempt reaches its normal end-of-action cleanup.","For the repeat example: a legal positive-PP ordinary Electric move is in the user’s current slots, normal gates pass, and a later ally uses legal Instruct after the user’s ordinary action; no special blacklist, locks, switching, fainting or host fault applies."],"minimal_counterexample":"Charge succeeds in round n: counter 2, then full round-tail 1. In round n+1 the user performs its normal Electric move: its initial damage reads positive Charge and receives the Charge power multiplier. The normal action end clears counter 1 to 0. A later ally’s Instruct repeats that Electric move in the same round, so the repeat reads 0 and receives no Charge multiplier. A timer-only implementation inferred from WP44 keeps 1 through both actions until the round tail and boosts the repeat incorrectly.","ordinary_control":"Immediately after newly setting Charge to 2, reaching that same action’s end leaves it 2; this is distinct from the count-1 clear. Another independent control removes Instruct and still observes the counter clear after the ordinary action.","cancellation_or_partial_commitment":"Successful first damage, PP and history stay committed; a later repeat does not undo them. A failed ordinary attempt that reaches the same end cleanup also clears the remaining count. A fault or branch that does not reach the cleanup has no automatic clear guarantee.","needed_consumer":"The exact end-of-action count-1 clear is needed in addition to WP43’s positive-count multiplier and WP42’s decrement; current WP40 mentions only an unspecified charge-remnant cleanup.","negative_searches":[{"paths":["deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-statuses-stat-stages-and-immunities.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-effect-coverage.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/pokemon-rules-wp43-44-46-48-50.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp40-commands-obedience-and-action-order.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp42-growth-end-of-round-and-battle-outcomes.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp43-types-accuracy-and-damage.md"],"terms":["Charge","充电","蓄力残段"],"result":"WP44 body fully read; catalog fully read; focused cross-owner search found establishment, positive power multiplier, tail decrement, and WP40’s unspecific cleanup label, but no explicit count-1 clear or repeat regression."}],"minimal_revision":"Add the reached action-end rule: if remaining Charge is exactly 1, clear it before later repeated-move consumers. Keep the existing 2 establishment, tail decrement, failure-stage and execution caveats. Name the exact rule at WP40’s cleanup handoff.","preserved_scope":["No new Charge duration or persistent field design.","No change to the default positive Charge multiplier or round-tail decrement.","No claim about runtime media, host recovery, or every exceptional callback."],"synchronization_files":["deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-statuses-stat-stages-and-immunities.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-effect-coverage.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/pokemon-rules-wp43-44-46-48-50.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp40-commands-obedience-and-action-order.md"],"acceptance_regression":["Establish 2, same-action cleanup preserves 2.","Full round tail reduces 2 to 1.","Reached ordinary action cleanup changes 1 to 0 regardless of move type or damage success.","A successful Electric move then same-round legal Instruct has Charge multiplier only on the first use.","An earlier fault that does not reach action cleanup is a separately conditional case."],"dependencies":["WP40 reached action cleanup and repeat execution","WP43 Charge multiplier","WP42 round-tail decrement","WP47-B Instruct entry conditions"],"rebuttal_target":"Show an existing frozen formal clause that already defines exactly 1→0 before repeated-move consumers, or show the legal repeat cannot occur under the listed conditions."}}
{"pointer":"/normative_records/13/original_full_proposal","prompt":"__ABSENT__","manifest":{"review_state":"SUSPECTED_PENDING_NON_PROPOSER_REBUTTAL_AND_ROOT_ADJUDICATION","evidence_class":"STATIC_REFERENCE_INSPECTION + DERIVED_VECTOR","execution":"NOT_EXECUTED","isolated_reference_execution":false,"independent_model_execution":false,"full_host_or_demo_execution":false,"proposer":"/root/cm_status_effects","severity_final":null,"non_proposer_rebuttal":{"status":"DONE","reviewer":"R6-CM/coordinator","recommendation":"SUPPORTED_WITH_SCOPE_NARROWING","artifact":"review/global-independent-review/sixth-2026-10-14-8ea169f-46ae/tasks/R6-CM/counter-R6-CM-SE-002.json"},"root_adjudication":{"status":"EXTERNAL_ROOT_PENDING","authority":"R6-I/global root; this task does not final-classify its own proposals"},"id":"R6-CM-SE-002","title":"Fang status immunity short-circuits the status random draw before the flinch draw","proposed_severity":"MEDIUM","source_locations":[{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/011_Battle/003_Move/007_MoveEffects_BattlerOther.rb","start":200,"end":212},{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/011_Battle/003_Move/007_MoveEffects_BattlerOther.rb","start":249,"end":261},{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/011_Battle/003_Move/007_MoveEffects_BattlerOther.rb","start":308,"end":320},{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/011_Battle/002_Battler/007_Battler_UseMove.rb","start":712,"end":719},{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/011_Battle/003_Move/003_Move_UsageCalculations.rb","start":489,"end":499},{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/011_Battle/002_Battler/004_Battler_Statuses.rb","start":25,"end":172},{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/PBS/moves.txt","start":1360,"end":1371}],"formal_locations":[{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-statuses-stat-stages-and-immunities.md","start":122,"end":122},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-effect-coverage.md","start":162,"end":162},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/pokemon-rules-wp43-44-46-48-50.md","start":37,"end":83}],"behavioral_fact":"Once a Fang secondary callback is actually reached and its internal chance is positive, it queries status eligibility first. Only an eligible status consumes its own status draw. The subsequent flinch draw is separate and still occurs when status is ineligible; it occurs before the Inner Focus rejection at flinch submission. The outer secondary-effect gate is a separate earlier draw; the default Thunder Fang outer chance is 101.","prerequisites":["Default Thunder Fang with ordinary command/PP/target checks passing.","The damage route reaches the secondary callback: calculated damage positive, no Sheer Force suppression, no active Shield Dust unless ignored, no substitute absorption.","Current mechanics use Electric-type paralysis immunity; actual target is pure Electric, remains alive, has no Inner Focus and no callback altering the status eligibility or counter.","No additional chance modifiers: internal chance 10. All earlier accuracy/critical/variance/outer draws fixed separately; the next two available internal random values are 5, then 99."],"minimal_counterexample":"Against an Electric target, paralysis eligibility is false before any status random draw. The first available internal random value 5 is consumed by flinch, so Flinch becomes true; 99 is not consumed inside that Fang callback. Reading “separately draw for status and flinch” as an unconditional pair instead consumes 5 on an impossible paralysis and 99 on flinch, producing false and shifting later random consumers.","ordinary_control":"With an otherwise identical target that is not paralysis-immune, internal 5 produces paralysis, then internal 99 does not flinch. If status submission immediately cures the new status, that submission and its cure callbacks still happened before the flinch draw. Another independent control has active Inner Focus: the flinch draw is still consumed, but its commit is rejected.","cancellation_or_partial_commitment":"The hit’s damage/PP/history are already committed before the internal callback. Immunity cancels only the status branch’s draw/commit, not the subsequent flinch draw. Status application and immediate cure are not rolled back by a later failed flinch commit.","needed_consumer":"Conditional random-consumption order needs the actual status query before the draw and the flinch commit after its own draw; two independent marginal chances alone do not define the sequence.","negative_searches":[{"paths":["deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-statuses-stat-stages-and-immunities.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-effect-coverage.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/pokemon-rules-wp43-44-46-48-50.md"],"ranges":{"WP44_body":[1,203],"WP44_coverage":[1,186],"shared_catalog":[1,246]},"terms":["牙类","Fang","分别抽取","免疫"],"result":"Full assigned formal text has two separate draws and component immunity, but does not specify the status-eligibility short circuit or a Fang internal random-consumption vector."}],"minimal_revision":"Qualify the Fang rule: query the chosen status first and draw its internal roll only if eligible; then independently draw for flinch and apply flinch’s own commit guard. Keep the distinct outer secondary gate and chance modifiers.","preserved_scope":["No claim that all secondary effects share Fang’s draw order.","No change to the 10% internal base chances or ordinary chance modifiers.","No runtime or global replay claim."],"synchronization_files":["deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-statuses-stat-stages-and-immunities.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/pokemon-rules-wp43-44-46-48-50.md"],"acceptance_regression":["Reached callback with status eligible: next internal 5,99 applies status, no flinch; two draws.","Reached callback with status immune: next internal 5,99 flinches; one internal draw, 99 remains for later consumer.","Positive chance and Inner Focus: draw consumed but flinch not committed.","Substitute, zero internal chance, or outer suppression skips the respective callback/draw path."],"dependencies":["WP43 probability helper and outer gate","WP44 status eligibility and flinch commit","WP40 damage-to-secondary stage order"],"rebuttal_target":"Demonstrate that the frozen formal wording already fixes conditional draw consumption, or that the listed default Thunder Fang callback cannot be reached."}}
