and-immunities.md","start":54,"end":54},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-statuses-stat-stages-and-immunities.md","start":124,"end":124},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-effect-coverage.md","start":162,"end":162},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/pokemon-rules-wp43-44-46-48-50.md","start":37,"end":83}],"behavioral_fact":"Psycho Shift target eligibility calls the generic status query directly. The rule module adds Sleep Clause/Modified Sleep Clause and Freeze Clause only to the dedicated sleep/freeze queries, not to that generic query. Sleep Talk can legally choose Psycho Shift and calls it through the special route, allowing an actually sleeping user to reach the transfer.","prerequisites":["Sleep Clause or Modified Sleep Clause is enabled and no later plugin replaces these queries.","User is sleeping with remaining count 2 before its ordinary Sleep Talk check; Sleep Talk reduces it to 1 but remains usable while asleep.","User knows legal Sleep Talk plus Psycho Shift; Psycho Shift is the only eligible called candidate, no contrary slot restrictions, no no-PP Sleep Talk failure.","Opposing target is alive, raw status NONE, with a different opposing non-egg party member already sleeping. Generic status guards pass: no substitute/protection, terrain/Uproar/status immunity, Prankster Dark restriction, reflection or callback affecting this example.","The target submission’s random sleep duration and any later cures are fixed separately; no held cure/ability cure exists in the minimal vector."],"minimal_counterexample":"The already sleeping opposing party member makes an ordinary direct sleep effect fail the dedicated Sleep Clause query. Under the same opposing party state, Sleep Talk calls Psycho Shift: generic status eligibility accepts the empty-status target, the target receives a newly chosen sleep duration, and the user is then cured. The same wrapper bypass exists structurally for transferring frozen status, without claiming a default ordinary frozen-user route.","ordinary_control":"Keep the target’s generic guards and party state identical, but use ordinary SleepTarget through its dedicated sleep query: the clause rejects it and no target sleep is committed. Independently clear the existing opposing sleep: dedicated sleep and the generic transfer can both pass their respective queries.","cancellation_or_partial_commitment":"Sleep Talk’s own PP and its initial sleep decrement are prior commitments. Called Psycho Shift uses special usage and does not consume a persistent Psycho Shift slot’s PP through the simple new-move route. Target status submission and its reactions precede the user cure; later cure/failure does not imply no target submission occurred.","needed_consumer":"The clause-wrapper consumer boundary must be distinguished from the generic eligibility used by Psycho Shift; declaring only “target must accept status” leaves the exception unresolved.","negative_searches":[{"paths":["deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-statuses-stat-stages-and-immunities.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-effect-coverage.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/pokemon-rules-wp43-44-46-48-50.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp47-a-move-attributes-targeting-and-calling.md"],"terms":["精神转移","GiveUserStatusToTarget","睡眠条款","冰冻条款"],"result":"WP44 body/effect coverage and full shared catalog freshly read; focused formal search found generic Psycho Shift acceptance plus ordinary clause descriptions, but no explicit Psycho Shift generic-query exception or regression."},{"paths":["reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/011_Battle/007_Other battle code/006_Battle_Clauses.rb","reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/011_Battle/002_Battler/004_Battler_Statuses.rb","reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/011_Battle/003_Move/007_MoveEffects_BattlerOther.rb"],"ranges":{"clauses":[58,101],"status":[25,172],"effect":[339,379]},"result":"Fresh exact-range inspection found wrappers for dedicated sleep, Yawn, freeze; no generic-query clause wrapper in the inspected rule block."}],"minimal_revision":"State in Psycho Shift’s bounded rule that it uses generic status eligibility and does not inherit the dedicated sleep/freeze clause wrapper. Add the ordinary direct sleep versus Sleep Talk→Psycho Shift control, leaving generic immunity/terrain/protection unchanged.","preserved_scope":["Retain specialized clause behavior on ordinary dedicated sleep/freeze and Yawn.","Do not assert all forced calls or debug submissions bypass all guards.","Do not invent a default frozen-user route."],"synchronization_files":["deliverables/final-specification-set/pokemon-rules/wp44-statuses-stat-stages-and-immunities.md","deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/pokemon-rules-wp43-44-46-48-50.md"],"acceptance_regression":["Enabled Sleep Clause, opposing reserve asleep, empty target: ordinary direct sleep rejected.","Same state, eligible Sleep Talk calls Psycho Shift: user sleep 2→1, target new sleep, user cured; outer PP remains spent.","Added generic terrain or immunity gate rejects transfer while keeping earlier Sleep Talk/PP commitments.","Target immediate cure case still registers the prior submission and subsequent user cure."],"dependencies":["WP44 generic status query and clause entry boundaries","WP47-A Sleep Talk pool and special call","WP40 special usage skip and PP/history","WP46/50 immediate cures and stage commitment"],"rebuttal_target":"Show an existing frozen formal exception for Psycho Shift’s clause-wrapper bypass or prove the listed ordinary Sleep Talk pool rejects Psycho Shift."}}
