y PP/history and initial whole-use admission, Protean changes current type to GHOST. The specific late Curse branch clears preselection and reconstructs a RandomNearFoe list, with fixed result seat3.","This branch calls the target-construction operation only. The next phase performs empty-list/initial success checks; it does not revisit redirection. Seat3 receives Curse and user HP becomes51, while seat1 remains uncursed despite Follow Me.","Applying the §5.1 normal construction-plus-redirection chain a second time would instead select seat1; that behavior is not the fixed-reference late branch."],"ordinary_control":["Change only the starting user current type to GHOST: initial target construction already uses RandomNearFoe, fixed choice seat3 is redirected by Follow Me to seat1, Protean does not alter the type, seat1 is cursed and user HP becomes51.","Remove only active Protean from the WATER-start fixture: initial target remains User/empty and the non-Ghost general effect requests Speed−1 then Attack+1 then Defense+1; no Curse HP cost and neither foe is cursed."],"partial_commits_under_cancellation":["At initial whole-use failure because all three non-Ghost stage requests are unavailable, ordinary PP/history are already committed, while the later Protean change/reconstruction/Curse/HP cost have not occurred.","Once the late Protean change has happened, it is not locally rolled back if the rebuilt target is already cursed or if an unrelated later callback fails; ordinary PP/history and any reached type write remain.","For a successful Curse target main effect, the target mark precedes user HP expenditure and HP-item check. An exception/cancellation after a reached write does not justify undoing that prefix. This proposal does not specify host recovery, continued process execution or diagnostic retries."],"negative_search":{"fully_read_formal_ranges":[{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/combat-requirements/wp47-a-move-attributes-targeting-and-calling.md","