ruction capability. The existing critical-rate value satisfies name existence but is an array instance; the construction request fails before the fallback branch. This differs from an absent legally queryable name.","minimal_counterexample":"Registered Physical/Power40 data with code CRITICAL_HIT_RATIOS resolves the existing array value, then fails the constructor request (NoMethodError class under ordinary Ruby receiver semantics). Status/Power0 fails at the same construction boundary; neither reaches whole-use fallback failure/damage. The claim remains pending independent validation of the exact valid-data premise and whether WP43 absence wording already excludes this named-but-nonconstructible case.","ordinary_control":"Only change code to absent ReviewMissingEffect: factory chooses Unimplemented; valid status then fails at whole-use gate, valid Physical40 continues common damage. Code None independently constructs the known ordinary no-extra-effect behavior.","failure_cancel_partial_commit":"Factory failure occurs before the constructed move can be used. Direct conversion has no move-use PP/damage commit. A simple called entrance attempts construction before its own pbUseMove call; outer caller PP/history/random choices may already be committed, but they require their own concrete caller fixture and are not automatically rolled back. No host crash/retry/recovery result is claimed.","negative_search_scope":{"source":"All13 primary source files newly read; only known critical-rate array binding and common factory are needed. Primary function-code binding table has401 default codes and no missing definition, so this does not allege default corruption.","formal":"WP43 full1–188 and complete shared catalog1–246 newly read; R5 fallback distinguishes nil/None/illegal query name/plugins, but no explicit existing nonconstructible-binding branch was located.","unverified":"No compiler/runtime execution performed. Nonproposer must inspect legal author data and guard interp