g/absent names and Array-instance lack of public construction in local Ruby2.6.10, not actual host behavior."},"concrete_caller_control":{"fixture":"A normal valid battle user knows default METRONOME, with remaining PP5 and no Pressure/choice/status/ability/item/other move-blocking obstacles. Add one uniquely registered author move only to the global content registry, not any active party move slot, with NORMAL type, valid target, Accuracy100, TotalPP5, no CannotMetronome/Shadow flags, FunctionCode CRITICAL_HIT_RATIOS; independently use Physical/Power40 or Status/Power0. Fix the first Metronome registry-key draw to this identity. All preconstruction feedback/animation returns normally. This is a static fixture, never registered or run here.","valid_entrance":"Metronome filters exact blacklist identity, CannotMetronome and original Shadow type. The collision code is outside the freshly read blacklist and the other two filters are absent, so it can be selected before temporary construction.","ordered_expected_prefix":["Ordinary outer METRONOME PP changes5→4; outer user/global use history is recorded as METRONOME.","The fixed registry draw selects the author move identity and stores it as the metronome selection.","Outer general effect enters simple use, which first constructs Pokemon::Move data successfully from the valid registry record.","Combat conversion resolves the existing Array binding and fails its construction request. It does not take the absent-binding Unimplemented branch. No inner pbUseMove has begun, and the temporary negative-PP assignment has not been reached."],"partial_commits_and_cancellation":"Outer PP/history and the reached selection are not locally rolled back by this failing call. The outer per-hit method has not normally returned, so its subsequent successful-hit increment, after-all-hits/end-of-use/ordinary end-turn completion cannot be invented. This states only the reached source prefix; outer diagnostic retry/recovery/host termination remains unverified.","ordinary_controls":["Change only the code to absent ReviewMissingEffect: conversion enters Unimplemented; Status0 then fails its own whole-use gate, while Physical40 reaches ordinary common damage if all remaining input guards permit.","Change only the code to known None: the ordinary no-extra-effect object is constructed, with subsequent outcome governed by its category/common rules.","The collision Physical40 and Status0 examples share the same earlier construction failure because category is not read to choose the missing-binding fallback branch."]}}}
